## Q4. Starvation Debugging

### Cause

Process **P5** is in the **lowest-priority queue (Q3)**.

Since higher-priority queues (**Q1** and **Q2**) continuously receive processes, Q3 never gets CPU time.

This causes **starvation**.

### Optimization

Use **Aging**.

Increase the priority of a process that waits for a long time so it eventually moves to a higher-priority queue and receives CPU time.

**Result:** Starvation is eliminated, and all processes get a fair chance to execute.

